  "name": "PT PROCESS PARAMETERS CHECK SHEET1",
  "logNumber": 171,
  "description": "Pre-Treatment _PT in a Paint Shop is a crucial process that prepares the metal surface for painting by removing oil, grease, rust, scale, and other contaminants and by creating a suitable surface for paint adhesion. The process typically involves cleaning, degreasing, water rinsing, surface conditioning, phosphating or other conversion coating, followed by rinsing and drying. Pre-treatment improves paint adhesion, corrosion resistance, and overall coating durability, resulting in a high-quality and long-lasting painted surface.",
