  },
  "name": "ED PROCESS PARAMETERS CHECK SHEET",
  "logNumber": 18,
  "description": "Electrodeposition (ED) coating in a paint shop is a crucial process used to apply a uniform and corrosion-resistant paint coating to metal components. In this process, the cleaned and pre-treated metal body is immersed in an electrically conductive paint bath, and an electrical current is applied to deposit the paint uniformly onto the metal surface, including difficult-to-reach areas. The deposited coating is then rinsed and cured in an oven to achieve the required film properties. ED coating provides excellent corrosion protection, uniform coating thickness, good adhesion, and a durable base for subsequent painting processes.",
  "documentNumber": "DICV _ED _002",
  "assetId": "69a043dc5dd07d06e4f199c6",
